mcp-server-wazuh (1.0.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * search_vulnerabilities: sort by vulnerability.detected_at. The
    wazuh-states-vulnerabilities index has no @timestamp, so every call
    failed with "No mapping found for [@timestamp] in order to sort on".
  * Sort with unmapped_type=date so an index lacking the sort field no
    longer fails the whole search.
  * agent_id filter: match wazuh.agent.id (Wazuh 5 data streams) as well
    as agent.id. The filter returned nothing on events and findings.

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 10:45:00 +0100

mcp-server-wazuh (1.0.0-3) unstable; urgency=low

  * Depend on python3-fastmcp (>= 4.0.10). The testing repository publishes
    4.0.10.38~trixie, so (>= 4.1.4) made the package uninstallable and the
    unit test then failed with "mcp-server-wazuh: not found".
  * Fail the Jenkins test stage when apt-get install fails.

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0100

